  "weekStart": "",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Quality vs. cost of the `prompt-file` feature flag.** Every request to `GET /test/prompt-score` evaluates `prompt-file` for a random user, scores the served prompt variant (**unreliable 0 · brief 3 · casual 5 · expert 10**) and draws a simulated model cost (cheapest for *unreliable*, most expensive for *expert*). Both are reported through the OpenFeature **tracking API** — `Track(\"prompt-score\")` and `Track(\"prompt-cost\")` — and exported as OpenTelemetry metrics.\n\n**Try it:** start the `k6-prompt-score` resource in the Aspire dashboard, then edit `src/Garage.AppHost/flags/flagd.json` — change the `defaultVariant` of `prompt-file` or add a `fractional` targeting rule — and watch quality and cost move. Hover the ⓘ icon on any panel for how it is computed and how to read it."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Average Prompt Score",
      "description": "Average quality score of the `prompt-file` variants being served right now, on a 0–10 scale (unreliable 0 · brief 3 · casual 5 · expert 10).\n\nComputed from the `prompt-score` OpenFeature tracking events as rate(sum) ÷ rate(count) over the rate interval, so it is weighted by traffic. Colour thresholds: red < 2.5, orange < 4.5, yellow < 7.5, green ≥ 7.5.\n\nChange `defaultVariant` or the targeting of `prompt-file` in `flagd.json` and this value follows within about a minute.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": "$metrics_ds",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(feature_flag_tracking_value_sum{feature_flag_tracking_event_name=\"prompt-score\"}[$__rate_interval])) / sum(rate(feature_flag_tracking_value_count{feature_flag_tracking_event_name=\"prompt-score\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "Score"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "min": 0,
          "max": 10,
          "decimals": 2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 2.5
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 4.5
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 7.5
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Tracking Events",
      "description": "Rate of `prompt-score` tracking events per second — one per request handled by `GET /test/prompt-score`.\n\nWith the `k6-prompt-score` load generator running this sits at ~10/s. If it reads 0, start the generator from the Aspire dashboard.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": "$metrics_ds",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(feature_flag_tracking_events_total{feature_flag_tracking_event_name=\"prompt-score\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "Events/s"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "green"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "piechart",
      "title": "Variant Share (last 5m)",
      "description": "Which `prompt-file` variants users actually received in the last five minutes, and in what proportion, counted from the tracking events (legend values are request counts).\n\nA single slice means everyone gets the default variant; several slices mean targeting — for example a `fractional` rollout rule — is splitting traffic.",
